 643:main.c        **** //		timing falls within these limits before the timing is applied.
 644:main.c        **** // My Notes:
 645:main.c        **** //  This does not seem to be implemented in any of the displays 
 646:main.c        **** //  I've checked.
 647:main.c        **** //  Nor is it mentioned in SPWG
 648:main.c        **** //But E-EDID mentions it twice!
 649:main.c        **** // 1) All blocks shall be filled with valid data using the formats
 650:main.c        **** //		described in sections 3.10.2 and 3.10.3.  Use of a data 
 651:main.c        **** //		fill pattern is not permitted. 
 652:main.c        **** // 2) Timing data must represent a supported mode of the display. 
 653:main.c        **** //	3) Descriptor blocks shall be ordered such that all detailed timing
 654:main.c        **** //		blocks precede other  types of descriptor blocks 
 655:main.c        **** //	4) The first descriptor block shall be used to indicate the display's
 656:main.c        **** //		preferred timing mode.  This is described in section 3.10.1 
 657:main.c        **** //	5) A Monitor Range Limits Descriptor must be provided 
 658:main.c        **** //	6) A Monitor Name Descriptor must be provided 
 659:main.c        **** //Note:  Items 4, 5 and 6 above were permitted but not required prior to 
 660:main.c        **** //		EDID structure version 1 revision 3.  Hosts may encounter displays 
 661:main.c        **** //		using EDID version 1 revision 0-2 which do not meet all of these 
 662:main.c        **** //		requirements.
